{"doc_id": "mb_2026_canola_insect_scouting_semantic_0001", "title": "Manitoba 2026 field-scouting design and threshold meaning", "text": "Field scouting is a repeated measurement process, not a single look from the field edge. Manitoba's 2026 guide recommends weekly checks during the growing season and more frequent checks when populations approach economic levels or weather favours rapid development. Sample at least five sites in a typical field, using an X, Z, or W path for broadly distributed insects and extra edge sampling for pests that concentrate near margins. Combine sweep-net observations with direct plant and soil-surface inspection. An economic threshold is the population or injury level at which action is considered before damage reaches the economic injury level; a nominal threshold is an experience-based decision guide. Crop stage, moisture, temperature, stand density, expected crop value, and control cost can change the interpretation.", "source": "https://www.gov.mb.ca/agriculture/crops/guides-and-publications/", "source_id": "mb_2026_canola_insect_scouting", "download_url": "https://www.gov.mb.ca/agriculture/crops/guides-and-publications/pubs/guide-crop-protection-insects-2026.pdf", "publisher": "Manitoba Agriculture", "license": "redistributable", "license_snapshot": {"status": "redistributable", "identifier": "OpenMB Information and Data Use Licence", "evidence_url": "https://www.gov.mb.ca/legal/copyright.html", "reviewed_on": "2026-07-24", "attribution": "Contains information from the Manitoba government, licensed under the OpenMB Information and Data Use Licence (Manitoba.ca/OpenMB).", "permits_modification": true, "permits_commercial": true, "permits_redistribution": true}, "sft_status": "unknown", "source_type": "applied_guidance", "document_type": "current_provincial_crop_scouting_guide", "format": "pdf", "region": ["Manitoba"], "jurisdiction": ["Manitoba"], "language": ["en-CA"], "currency": {"status": "current_2026_edition", "review_interva