{"doc_id": "mb_2026_crop_disease_scouting_semantic_0001", "title": "Manitoba 2026 cereal leaf disease and Fusarium head blight scouting", "text": "For Manitoba cereals in the 2026 season, inspect fields before, during, and after flag-leaf emergence because the flag and upper leaves supply at least half of grain fill. Fusarium head blight risk is driven strongly by weather during flowering: the guide identifies sustained moisture for roughly 48 to 60 hours with temperatures from 15 to 30 degrees Celsius as favourable conditions. Rotation away from cereals, grasses, and corn for at least one year and preferably two can reduce residue-borne risk, but cannot override conducive weather. Use clean seed and current provincial variety resistance ratings. Scouting and weather observations establish risk; they do not confirm mycotoxin concentration, authorize a product, or replace a current pesticide label.", "source": "https://www.gov.mb.ca/agriculture/crops/guides-and-publications/", "source_id": "mb_2026_crop_disease_scouting", "download_url": "https://www.gov.mb.ca/agriculture/crops/guides-and-publications/pubs/guide-crop-protection-diseases-2026.pdf", "publisher": "Manitoba Agriculture", "license": "redistributable", "license_snapshot": {"status": "redistributable", "identifier": "OpenMB Information and Data Use Licence", "evidence_url": "https://www.gov.mb.ca/legal/copyright.html", "reviewed_on": "2026-07-24", "attribution": "Contains information from the Manitoba government, licensed under the OpenMB Information and Data Use Licence (Manitoba.ca/OpenMB).", "permits_modification": true, "permits_commercial": true, "permits_redistribution": true}, "sft_status": "unknown", "source_type": "applied_guidance", "document_type": "current_provincial_crop_scouting_guide", "format": "pdf", "region": ["Manitoba"], "jurisdiction": ["Manitoba"], "language": ["en-CA"], "currency": {"status": "current_2026_edition", "review_interval_days": 90, "volatile": true}, "regulatory": {"regula