{"doc_id": "mb_2026_crop_disease_scouting_semantic_0002", "title": "Manitoba 2026 canola clubroot recognition and containment", "text": "Suspect clubroot in Manitoba canola when patches show wilting, stunting, yellowing, premature ripening, or shrivelled seed, especially near field entrances where contaminated soil may first arrive. Confirm the field symptom by digging plants and checking roots for galls; submit symptomatic plants to a qualified laboratory when confirmation matters. Warm, wet, acidic soils favour disease, but clubroot can occur outside those conditions. Resting spores move with eroded soil, water, animals or manure, footwear, tires, and soil attached to equipment, and a small fraction can persist for up to 20 years. Rotation, resistant varieties, regular scouting, and preventing soil movement are complementary controls; no single observation establishes field-wide severity.", "source": "https://www.gov.mb.ca/agriculture/crops/guides-and-publications/", "source_id": "mb_2026_crop_disease_scouting", "download_url": "https://www.gov.mb.ca/agriculture/crops/guides-and-publications/pubs/guide-crop-protection-diseases-2026.pdf", "publisher": "Manitoba Agriculture", "license": "redistributable", "license_snapshot": {"status": "redistributable", "identifier": "OpenMB Information and Data Use Licence", "evidence_url": "https://www.gov.mb.ca/legal/copyright.html", "reviewed_on": "2026-07-24", "attribution": "Contains information from the Manitoba government, licensed under the OpenMB Information and Data Use Licence (Manitoba.ca/OpenMB).", "permits_modification": true, "permits_commercial": true, "permits_redistribution": true}, "sft_status": "unknown", "source_type": "applied_guidance", "document_type": "current_provincial_crop_scouting_guide", "format": "pdf", "region": ["Manitoba"], "jurisdiction": ["Manitoba"], "language": ["en-CA"], "currency": {"status": "current_2026_edition", "review_interval_days": 90, "volatile": true}, "regulatory": {"regulated_adv